<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · conquest</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russian conquest of Siberia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1581">1581</a>–<a href="/years/1778">1778</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russian conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siberia">Siberia</a> took place between 1581 and 1778, beginning traditionally with the campaign of some 540 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yermak-timofeyevich">Yermak Timofeyevich</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khanate-of-sibir">Khanate of Sibir</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuchum">Kuchum Khan</a>. Yermak entered its capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qashliq">Qashliq</a>, in 1582 but was defeated in 1584; the Russians returned in 1586, and Kuchum Khan was beaten at the Battle of Irmen in 1598. From forts built to collect yasak, a fur tribute, the Russians pushed east and reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pacific-ocean">Pacific Ocean</a> in 1639. The indigenous peoples resisted, the Cossacks often committed atrocities against them, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> carried away up to 80 percent of the Tungus and Yakut populations in the 1650s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/russian-conquest-of-siberia.jpg" alt="Russian conquest of Siberia" width="330" height="157" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vasiliy Surikov · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Surikov_Pokoreniye_Sibiri_Yermakom.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
